  "solutions": [
    {
      "id": "sol.ahsme-1974-p15.live",
      "kind": "proof-sketch",
      "text": "Since \\(x\\lt-2,\\) \\(1+x\\lt0,\\) so \\(|1+x|=-1-x.\\) Thus \\(\\bigl|1-|1+x|\\bigr|\\) becomes \\(|1-(-1-x)|,\\) which is \\(|2+x|=-2-x\\) because \\(2+x\\lt0.\\)\n\nTherefore, the correct answer is B.",
      "hints": [
        "Resolve the inner absolute value first using \\(1+x\\lt-1\\)",
        "After replacing \\(|1+x|\\) by \\(-1-x,\\) determine the sign of \\(2+x\\)"
      ],
      "images": []
    }
